            <ArticleTitle>Prognostic significance of cerebrovascular and peripheral arterial disease in patients having percutaneous coronary interventions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1536-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study shows that cerebrovascular and peripheral arterial diseases frequently co-exist in patients with coronary artery disease who undergo percutaneous coronary interventions. These 2 conditions are associated with adverse in-hospital and 1-year outcomes and independently predict early and 1-year mortality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
